-- supabase/provision-identity.sql.template
-- ============================================================================
-- THE STEP A FRESHLY BUILT DATABASE CANNOT SERVE TRAFFIC WITHOUT.
--
-- Found by the staging integration gate on its first execution: 39 of 49 route
-- assertions returned 503 with
--
--     BINDING_INVALID {"code":"identity_not_provisioned","target":"preview"}
--
-- The chain, and every link in it is behaving correctly:
--   * 0050 creates deployment_identity and set_deployment_identity(), revoked from
--     public, anon and authenticated.
--   * 0051 re-grants execute on public functions to service_role but DELIBERATELY
--     excludes set_deployment_identity, so a running request can never rewrite which
--     environment the database claims to be. That exclusion is a security property and
--     is kept.
--   * `supabase db reset` leaves deployment_identity EMPTY.
--   * api/_env.js treats an unprovisioned identity as a FAILURE rather than as
--     unknown-but-fine. Also correct: fail closed.
--
-- The consequence is operational, not a bug in any one of those pieces: a database
-- built from the migration chain serves ZERO requests until an operator provisions the
-- identity through a privileged channel the application itself cannot reach.
--
-- That matters directly for the production cutover Codex ordered -- a FRESH production
-- project. Without this step the sequence is: create project, apply migrations, deploy,
-- and 503 on every request with a message that names no cause.
--
-- WHY A TEMPLATE, AND WHY IT IS RENDERED RATHER THAN PARAMETERISED:
--   `supabase db query -f` takes no bind parameters. Hardcoding a project ref would put
--   an environment-specific literal in the repository and invite exactly the copy-paste
--   accident this project has spent weeks eliminating. So the ref is substituted at run
--   time by .github/scripts/provision-identity.sh, which refuses any ref that is not the
--   approved target.
--
-- THIS IS NOT TEST SCAFFOLDING. CI runs the same rendered statement an operator runs at
-- production cutover. Hiding it inside the test harness would have made the suite pass
-- while leaving the cutover runbook silently incomplete -- a green check standing in for
-- a step nobody had written down.
-- ============================================================================

select public.set_deployment_identity(
  '__ENVIRONMENT__',
  '__PROJECT_REF__',
  'provisioned by CI after clean build'
);
